From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 04:16:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath11k: backport 18 upstream fixes

backports-7.2 predates these ath11k fixes, merged upstream from July to
October 2026 (torvalds/linux):

  12b09e478aa7 cap out-of-range rx MCS instead of leaving bogus rate
  9ef9dd30058c Avoid buffer overread in ath11k_wmi_tlv_op_rx()
  6fe2dddf59bb Correctly copy the hint BSSID in WMI scan request
  f8729a40ebcc validate regulatory capability phy_id
  208d7fdb8597 fix overreads in ath11k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event()
  7a246c72132e fix stride mismatch in mac_phy_caps_parse()
  0293be2212d3 fix leak in ath11k_service_ready_ext_event()
  1a7bcf5324c8 fix NULL dereference in ahb remove when QMI init incomplete
  1d8e73163ef9 unregister PM notifier on QMI init failure path
  6132d70d0890 Fix possible memory leak in ath11k_dp_srng_setup()
  c7555d47b1d0 fix locking problem in ath11k_dp_rx_tid_del_func()
  52953d149ab4 modify null check logic in ath11k_ce_rx_post_pipe()
  820b8cff81c7 cleanup arsta in ath11k_mac_peer_cleanup_all()
  7e0ad05ebc72 reset ar->num_stations on hardware start
  64828f091c7d fix reg_info_store leak in ath11k_service_ready_ext_event()
  170404d5e976 read wiphy regd under RCU
  3e7f5d362b2b avoid IDR mutation during pending mgmt TX cleanup
  dc29226dada3 avoid IDR mutation during vif mgmt TX cleanup

Among them: a QCN9074 crash in ath11k_dp_rx_tid_del_func() (list walked
with its lock dropped), num_stations not reset on hardware start (new
stations refused after restarts), WMI event overreads, leaks, and
out-of-range RX MCS reported as bogus rates. They apply as they are, in
upstream order, before the port's and OpenWrt's own ath11k patches, which
all still apply (offsets only). Not taken: e56c9d429ba0 (suspend/resume;
needs code 7.2 lacks), 8ab38bbac022 and 32ec8488d75d (contexts OpenWrt's
patches change).

Build-tested for ipq60xx (no new warnings); the three modules ran on the
W-318 (IPQ6018 + QCN9072). Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
